preConditionHook:
// GUARD (2026-09-17): a level's EXISTENCE is a bool set when the scan finds the
// SECOND pivot (haveLo / haveHi), never a test of the price against -1 -- a back-adjusted series can print
// -1.00 (or 0.00) as a real price. The EL twin guards on the bar index
// (SwingLowBar / SwingHighBar <> -1, VERIFIED), a count and not a price.
// Mentions of the -1 SENTINEL below describe what EL's SwingLow / SwingHigh
// return, not how this rule guards it.
// THE MINIMUM PRECONDITION FOR A WITH-TREND TRADE: the most recently CONFIRMED
// swing low is above the one before it -- a higher low. Brooks: "a trader
// usually should not be looking to buy unless the market is at least forming a
// higher low". Mirrored: the short side wants the most recent swing pivot high below
// the one before it, a lower high.
//
// Not LaggedHigherHigh, which compares two ADJACENT BARS at a fixed lag on the
// opposite series, and not HigherLowCount, which counts adjacent-bar pairs. This
// reads the STRUCTURE -- two confirmed pivots, however many bars apart -- which
// no fixed-lag bar comparison reaches. The cheap window proxy the merge recorded
// (lowest(low, n) now against lowest(low, n) n bars ago) is a different test and
// is not used.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS INLINED from SwingHigh per the B-list decision -- rules in
// this corpus never reference each other -- and mirrors the twin's SwingLow /
// SwingHigh at Occurrence 1 and 2. Scanning newest-first and taking the first
// two hits is what reproduces those two occurrences. MEASURED
// (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min):
//   * the pivot test is MIXED: at-or-beyond the strength OLDER bars, STRICTLY
//     beyond the strength NEWER bars. Bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER index
//     the NEWER bar, so the strict half is the pk < pj loop;
//   * the confirmation lag is exactly strength bars, never 0 or 1, so the scan
//     is lookahead-safe, and during the lag it reports the PREVIOUS pivot;
//   * maxBarsBack is EL's Length: candidate offsets 0..maxBarsBack-1 from the
//     current bar INCLUSIVE, and the neighbourhood test reaches strength bars
//     PAST the window, so the deepest bar touched is maxBarsBack - 1 + strength;
//   * fewer than two pivots in the window is the -1 SENTINEL case, guarded on
//     BOTH occurrences because -1 as a PRICE sits under every real price and
//     would otherwise read as a higher low;
//   * the comparisons carry the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance, hence el_lt /
//     el_le / el_gt / el_ge inside the scan rather than raw operators.
// The low side's tie sense is the mirror of the measured high-side rule, not an
// observation. Occurrence 3+ is unmeasured and is not asked for. No
// WFSafe_SwingLow exists, so plain EL governs.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope
// declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement.
lo1 = 0.0;
lo2 = 0.0;
haveLo = false;
foundLo = 0;
for (pj = (int)strength; pj <= (int)maxBarsBack - 1; ++pj) {
    pok = true;
    for (pk = pj - (int)strength; pk < pj; ++pk) {
        if (!el_lt(low[pj], low[pk])) { pok = false; break; }
    }
    if (pok) {
        for (pk = pj + 1; pk <= pj + (int)strength; ++pk) {
            if (!el_le(low[pj], low[pk])) { pok = false; break; }
        }
    }
    if (pok) {
        ++foundLo;
        if (foundLo == 1) { lo1 = low[pj]; }
        else { lo2 = low[pj]; haveLo = true; break; }
    }
}
hi1 = 0.0;
hi2 = 0.0;
haveHi = false;
foundHi = 0;
for (pj = (int)strength; pj <= (int)maxBarsBack - 1; ++pj) {
    pok = true;
    for (pk = pj - (int)strength; pk < pj; ++pk) {
        if (!el_gt(high[pj], high[pk])) { pok = false; break; }
    }
    if (pok) {
        for (pk = pj + 1; pk <= pj + (int)strength; ++pk) {
            if (!el_ge(high[pj], high[pk])) { pok = false; break; }
        }
    }
    if (pok) {
        ++foundHi;
        if (foundHi == 1) { hi1 = high[pj]; }
        else { hi2 = high[pj]; haveHi = true; break; }
    }
}
